#=GF TP   Domain
#=GF CL   CL0084
#=GF RN   [1]
#=GF RM   26749446
#=GF RT   The Structure of the Toxin and Type Six Secretion System
#=GF RT   Substrate Tse2 in Complex with Its Immunity Protein.
#=GF RA   Robb CS, Robb M, Nano FE, Boraston AB;
#=GF RL   Structure. 2016;24:277-284.
#=GF DR   INTERPRO; IPR041018;
#=GF DR   SO; 0000417; polypeptide_domain;
#=GF CC   Tse2 from P. aeruginosa has structural features similar to
#=GF CC   ADP-ribosylating toxins. It is a cytoactive toxin secreted by a
#=GF CC   type six secretion apparatus of Pseudomonas aeruginosa and found
#=GF CC   mostly in gamma proteobacteria. It naturally attacks a target in
#=GF CC   the cytoplasm of bacterial cells. Structural analysis shows
#=GF CC   similarity between Tse2 and nicotinamide adenine dinucleotide
#=GF CC   (NAD)-dependent enzymes from bacteria, notably the
#=GF CC   mono-ADP-ribosyltransferase toxins (ADPRTs). Furthermore, it
#=GF CC   revealed that the Tse2 active site is occluded upon binding the
#=GF CC   cognate immunity protein Tsi2. The abrogation of toxicity for
#=GF CC   the R14A, S80A, and H122A mutant Tse2 proteins indicates the
#=GF CC   importance of these amino acids in the mechanism of Tse2
#=GF CC   toxicity and, given their conservation with NAD-reactive
#=GF CC   enzymes, also supports their assignment as being involved in a
#=GF CC   catalytic reaction [1].
#=GF SQ   412
